To optimize GridPass pages for 2026, we'll implement a structured approach focusing on titles, descriptions, Open Graph tags, keywords, and code style. Here's the organized solution:

### Title Optimization
- **Format**: Use "Page Topic | GridPass" or dynamic "Entity Name | GridPass Profile".
- **Example**: If it's about iRacing, use "iRacing Management | GridPass Profile".

### Description Optimization
- **Length**: Under 110 characters.
- **Content**: Concise summary highlighting key points and benefits.

### Open Graph Tags
- **Type**: Use "website" for general pages, "profile" for profile-specific ones.
- **Site Name**: Always include "GridPass".
- **Image**: Include user avatar or vehicle image for profiles; use specific assets or default image for static pages.

### AI & Semantic Search
- **Clarity**: Ensure titles and descriptions clearly define the page content.
- **Keywords**: Integrate "Sim Racing", "Management", "iRacing", "Motorsport", and "Team Logistics" naturally into metadata.

### Code Implementation

import type { Metadata } from 'next';

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: { 
  topic: string;
  name?: string; // For profile pages
}) {
  const pageTopic = params.topic || 'Home';
  const entityName = params.name || undefined;

  return metadata({
    title: `Page Topic | GridPass`,
    description: `Summary of Page Topic for GridPass`,
    keywords: ['Sim Racing', 'Management', 'iRacing', 'Motorsport', 'Team Logistics'],
    ogType: params.type || 'website',
    ogSiteName: 'GridPass',
    ogImage: params.name ? `/images/og-profile.jpg` : '/images/og-default.jpg',
  });
}

function HomePage() {
  return (
    <div className="container">
      <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold">Home</h1>
      {/* Include generated metadata using generateMetadata */}
    </div>
  );
}

function PageEntity(params) {
  return (
    <div className="container">
      {generateMetadata(params)} // Pass params to include entity-specific data
    </div>
  );
}


